The diagram shows one activity from a project. The completed scan boxes contain EST on the left and LST on the right. Times are in hours.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (U) at (0,0);\coordinate (V) at (5,0);
\draw[->] (U)--(V) node[midway,above=5pt] {$A,\,4$};
\fill (U) circle (2pt);\fill (V) circle (2pt);
\draw (-0.6,0.5) rectangle (0.6,1.1);\draw (0,0.5)--(0,1.1);
\node at (-0.3,0.8) {$2$};\node at (0.3,0.8) {$5$};
\draw (4.4,0.5) rectangle (5.6,1.1);\draw (5,0.5)--(5,1.1);
\node at (4.7,0.8) {$8$};\node at (5.3,0.8) {$11$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Calculate the total float of activity $A$ and state whether it is critical.

The forward and backward scans are complete. Each box contains EST on the left and LST on the right. Durations are in days; the dashed edge is a dummy activity of duration $0$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (S) at (0,0);\coordinate (U) at (2.5,1.5);\coordinate (L) at (2.5,-1.5);\coordinate (V) at (5.2,1.5);\coordinate (W) at (5.2,-1.5);\coordinate (M) at (7.9,0);\coordinate (T) at (10.2,0);
\draw[->] (S)--(U) node[pos=0.6,above=6pt] {$A,\,6$};
\draw[->] (S)--(L) node[midway,below left] {$B,\,4$};
\draw[->] (U)--(V) node[midway,above] {$C,\,2$};
\draw[->] (L)--(W) node[midway,below] {$D,\,3$};
\draw[->,dashed] (V)--(W) node[midway,left=4pt] {$0$};
\draw[->] (V)--(M) node[midway,above right] {$E,\,4$};
\draw[->] (W)--(M) node[pos=0.4,below=6pt] {$F,\,2$};
\draw[->] (M)--(T) node[midway,above] {$G,\,3$};
\foreach \p in {S,U,L,V,W,M,T}{\fill (\p) circle (2pt);}
\node[left=4pt] at (S) {Start};\node[right=4pt] at (T) {Finish};
\foreach \x/\y/\e/\l in {0/0.9/0/0,2.5/2.3/6/6,2.5/-2.3/4/7,5.2/2.3/8/8,5.2/-2.3/8/10,7.9/-0.9/12/12,10.2/-0.9/15/15}{
\draw (\x-0.6,\y-0.3) rectangle (\x+0.6,\y+0.3);
\draw (\x,\y-0.3)--(\x,\y+0.3);
\node at (\x-0.3,\y) {$\e$};\node at (\x+0.3,\y) {$\l$};}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(a) Calculate the total float of every activity, including the dummy.
(b) Name the critical activities and count them.
(c) Identify the activities with a float of $3$ days and state which activities have the longest float.
